Z||000005||JohnnyK||03-15-2001||10:08 PM||||It seemed to me that the roof is a totally different part? It seems it stops, and another piece starts right above the rear window (this is a notchback, don't know if I'm making sense) and turns into another piece at the hood. I guess I can't undo all that somehow off both cars, and just plop them down on each other? I'll have to start cutting the insides eh?||||reg||1
Z||000006||tgowens||03-15-2001||10:24 PM||||While all Fieros are cut out in the top of the space frame for the sunroof, you would still need to cut the sides of the roof section of the space frame and weld in the center section.<P>As to the removal of the Enduroflex roof panel, it can be done easily in a couple of hours.........there are bolts thru from the inside and two at the base of the windshield.......||||reg||1
Z||000007||JohnnyK||03-15-2001||10:28 PM||||So it's more work than I thought eh.. crap||||reg||1
Z||000008||JohnnyK||03-15-2001||10:33 PM||||I just need someone to tell me exactly what I have to do to see if it's worth it (plausible in a few days). Two fiero's. An 84 WITH t-tops, and an 85se with a sunroof. I want to switch the two roofs (I would be keeping the 85se with the t-tops installed). What happens to the 84 is not as important, but it would be nice to put a roof on it and sell it. Someone help, as I have to decide tonight (ooh boy is he going to be mad).||||reg||1
Z||000009||skitime||03-15-2001||10:48 PM||||There will be cutting of the car recieving the T-top.  The car is cut across the front behind the windshield and across behind the doors. The car need to be reinforced during the installation as well to prevent it from slightly coming together between the windshield and rear pillars. The t-top is not welded in but pop riveted in so there is no welding. I don't see why it couldn't be done in a long day.  Measure twice cut once!||||reg||1
Z||000010||JohnnyK||03-15-2001||10:50 PM||||It actually sounds pretty easy, especially seeing as I'll have the t-top donar car to go by. Oh well, I'll sleep on it. Chances are I won't buy it though.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000011||skitime||03-15-2001||10:51 PM||||BTW, I fear that the donor car will be wasted unless you want to make a convertible.||||reg||1
Z||000012||DRH||03-15-2001||11:10 PM||||Johnny,<P>I've never done it so I can't give you instructions, but I do understand why everyone is telling you it's a BIG deal. I have seen a Fiero with the roof "skin" off. There is a solid steel piece of body underneath. It is all one piece or welded together all the way from the front of the car, around the windshield, around the back window, back to the back of the car. It has a big hole where the sunroof is but otherwise is one piece.<P>After pulling the skins off (this can be tricky to not break the narrow pieces next to the windshield). You have to cut out part of your roof and install the t-bar down the middle. I would think getting everything aligned would be very tricky... <P>Putting the sunroof top back on the t-top car will be all but impossible. You would have to weld the pieces cut out of your car back into it. You would probably never get it lined up right, plus it probably wouldn't be safe if it ever rolled over.<P>I don't think this is a job you want to try for the first time under a time constraint (if at all). Probably not what you want to hear... but that's my .02 worth of advise. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000013||onfire||03-16-2001||03:07 AM||||Hey I have an idea, why not take everything you like off the 85 and put it on the 84? Or not. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000014||Jay||03-16-2001||09:02 AM||||Johnnyk, I don't know if you are familiar with the Fiero Shop (Race-Tech) in Toronto, but if you want to talk to someone in person about it you should give them a call and ask for Joe.  He's got tons of Fiero's there and has done this kind of stuff before.  He might also be interested in buying that T-top Fiero.  Give him a call at 416-747-5728.  They also have a web sight at <A HREF="http://www.racetechauto.com" TARGET=_blank>www.racetechauto.com</A>   They specialize in Fieros, Cavaliers and Sunfires.||||reg||1
